# mangago.me requires a logged-in session to read a full chapter's pages in
# a single request. Anonymous readers get one HTTP request per panel instead
# of one per chapter (~50x more requests for a 50-page chapter), and
# anonymous traffic is more likely to hit mangago's Cloudflare bot challenge.
# See README.md ("Why mangago needs an account") for the full explanation.
#
# Create a free account at https://www.mangago.me/home/accounts/login/ and
# put its credentials here, then run:
#   python -m tests.mangago_login
# It opens a real (headless) Firefox instance, fills in these credentials,
# and saves the login captcha image to data/mangago_captcha.png -- mangago sits
# behind bot-management that a plain HTTP client can't satisfy, even with
# correct credentials, so a real browser is required. Whoever/whatever can
# read that image writes its text to data/.mangago_captcha_answer.txt; the
# waiting script picks that up, submits the form, confirms login, and writes
# the session to MANGAGO_COOKIE below, which is what the driver actually
# sends on every request. Only needs to be redone once that session
# expires, not on every run.
#
# Copy this file to .env (already gitignored) and fill in the real values.
# Never commit .env -- it holds your live credentials and session.
MANGAGO_EMAIL=
MANGAGO_PASSWORD=

# Populated automatically after a successful login. Leave blank initially.
MANGAGO_COOKIE=
